 <section aria-labelledby="academic-title" class="section academic-section shell" id="academic"><div class="section-top compact"><span class="overline">PHARMACEUTICAL RESEARCH</span><h2 id="academic-title">Science behind<br/><em>the systems thinking.</em></h2></div><div class="academic-grid"><article class="thesis-card"><div aria-hidden="true" class="thesis-preview"><span class="mini-kicker">M.PHARM / FORMULATION SCIENCE</span><span class="preview-title">DERMAL<br/>DELIVERY</span><span class="preview-flow">15 batches · 50+ samples · 12-hour evaluation</span></div><span class="mini-kicker">M.PHARM THESIS · JUL 2025–SEP 2026</span><h3>Ruxolitinib-loaded transfersomal gel for dermal delivery</h3><p>Developed and optimized 15 formulation batches and evaluated 50+ experimental samples. The supplied resume/CV reports up to 88.5% drug-entrapment efficiency, a 12-hour UV-Visible drug-release evaluation, selected particle-size, zeta-potential, FTIR and DSC characterization, and topical gel stability at 0, 30 and 90 days.</p><div class="thesis-metrics"><span><b>15</b> batches</span><span><b>50+</b> samples</span><span><b>88.5%</b> entrapment efficiency</span></div><small>The efficiency figure is not bioavailability or clinical effectiveness. Formal title and records should be confirmed before public publication.</small></article><div class="academic-side"><article id="conjunctivitis_review"><a aria-label="Open Conjunctivitis review academic document" class="academic-preview" data-document-title="Conjunctivitis review" href="./assets/docs/Conjunctivitis_Review.html" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><span class="mini-kicker">B.PHARM / ACADEMIC RESEARCH</span><span class="preview-title">CONJUNCTIVITIS<br/>REVIEW</span><span class="preview-flow">5 EVIDENCE DOMAINS</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="preview-arrow">↗</span></a><span class="mini-kicker">B.PHARM / 7TH SEMESTER</span><div class="academic-highlight"><strong>05</strong><span>EVIDENCE DOMAINS<small>ACADEMIC LITERATURE ANALYSIS</small></span></div><h3>Conjunctivitis review</h3><p>Synthesized literature across 5 evidence domains in a conjunctivitis review, producing a structured map linking disease causes with diagnostic and therapeutic considerations.</p><a class="academic-open" data-document-title="Conjunctivitis review" href="./assets/docs/Conjunctivitis_Review.html" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">OPEN ACADEMIC DOCUMENT <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article><article id="pharmaceutical_social_media_review"><a aria-label="Open Pharmaceutical social-media marketing academic document" class="academic-preview" data-document-title="Pharmaceutical social-media marketing" href="./assets/docs/Pharmaceutical_Social_Media_Review.html" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><span class="mini-kicker">B.PHARM / ACADEMIC RESEARCH</span><span class="preview-title">PHARMA<br/>COMMUNICATION</span><span class="preview-flow">4 RESEARCH THEMES</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="preview-arrow">↗</span></a><span class="mini-kicker">B.PHARM / 8TH SEMESTER</span><div class="academic-highlight"><strong>04</strong><span>RESEARCH THEMES<small>ACADEMIC LITERATURE ANALYSIS</small></span></div><h3>Pharmaceutical social-media marketing</h3><p>Analyzed pharmaceutical social-media practices across 4 themes — promotion, stakeholder engagement, regulatory risk and responsible communication — to develop an opportunity-versus-compliance framework.</p><a class="academic-open" data-document-title="Pharmaceutical social-media marketing" href="./assets/docs/Pharmaceutical_Social_Media_Review.html" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">OPEN ACADEMIC DOCUMENT <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article><p class="small-note">These are academic projects, not claimed peer-reviewed publications.</p></div></div></section>
 
